{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971622-updating-the-usiri-as-a-mummy-crossover-focused-bloodline","id":971622,"title":"Updating the Usiri as a Mummy crossover-focused bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T18:06:42-07:00","id":971622,"title":"Updating the Usiri as a Mummy crossover-focused bloodline","content":"So one of my all-time favorite Requiem books is the <i>Ancient Mysteries/Ancient Bloodlines</i> pair from 1e, because I'm a sucker for historical settings and the incredibly diversity inside those books blew me away. One thing that's saddened me is that the shift to 2e has invalidated a decent chunk of that content due to the removal of the Fog of Ages (though this thread isn't for arguing about that), not the least of which was a bloodline I really enjoyed: the Usiri! The Usiri were a Nosferatu bloodline primarily concerned with memory, specifically safeguarding the memories of torpid elders so that they could rise again later and beat the Fog of Ages by getting their memories back from one of these guys. While 2e still has confusing dreams and radical personality changes as possibilities during torpor, the removal of the Fog of Ages basically means that the Usiri now exist as an answer to a thread that isn't canon any more. I was ready to shelve them as a fun little 1e artifact until an evil thought struck me: who else is immortal, tied to Ancient Egypt, and struggle with unreliable Memory?<br /> <br /> The Usiri have a ready place as attendants to the Arisen of <i>Mummy: the Curse</i>. I've said before that vampires make ideal cultists for the Arisen, as unlike stupid mortals who do that whole dying thing you can count on the same vampire to hear your commands in one Descent and still be there to carry them out during the next one two centuries later. While the Judges aren't terribly fond of their servants rebuilding themselves (time spent building up Memory and having a sense of identity isn't spent delivering tasty artifacts into the dead clutches) and the Nameless Empire would almost certainly decry vampires as hated Lifeless to be struck down, there then exists a sort of strange grey market in the Arisen offering their mortal cultists as a ready herd for the Usiri in exchange for loyal service and the ability to retain Memory between descents.<br /> <br /> Where I'm stumbling with all this is the mechanical side of things. While the 1e version of the Usiri had a custom Discipline, Hypnagogia, aimed at stealing, rewriting, and deleting memories (along with one sort of inexplicable power that helps other resist Frenzy, which I did like but was a flavor misstep), a lot of this was both adversarial in nature and has been subsumed into 2e's rules for Dominate anyway. I'm less interested in powers that steal or rewrite memories and would like to focus instead on the ability to bank and imprint them onto people, whether amnesiac mummies or even just mortals. I'm looking for something more complex than just &quot;succeed on your roll and either the Arisen's Memory increases by 1 for free or the target automatically resolves the Amnesia or False Memories Conditions&quot; and with some more nuance.<br /> <br /> Can anybody lend a helping hand here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:19:53-07:00","id":971629,"title":"","content":"Hm, what do we have on how Arisen powers interact with vampires? That's another thing to consider. <br /> <br /> The B+S Bloodline design philosophy seems to be to add a fourth Discipline and a new Bloodline &quot;Gift&quot;, which can be a power or set of Devotions, so I don't think they need an entire new Discipline. As for the fourth Discipline they get, I'm thinking either Dominate or Auspex. Their Gift could be a set of Devotions based on either of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:27:10-07:00","id":971635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971622-updating-the-usiri-as-a-mummy-crossover-focused-bloodline?p=971629#post971629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, what do we have on how Arisen powers interact with vampires? That's another thing to consider.<br /> <br /> The B+S Bloodline design philosophy seems to be to add a fourth Discipline and a new Bloodline &quot;Gift&quot;, which can be a power or set of Devotions, so I don't think they need an entire new Discipline. As for the fourth Discipline they get, I'm thinking either Dominate or Auspex. Their Gift could be a set of Devotions based on either of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dominate seems to be the given Discipline for fucking with memories, so a Auspex/Dominate/Nightmare/Obfuscate spread seems perfectly fitting. Their power work well as Auspex/Dominate combination Devotions, but the actual mechanical meat behind that is eluding me; Memory is bought up with Experience rather than rolled for, which is where the whole helping aspect seems to stumble.<br /> <br /> Maybe they can bank a point of Memory per <i>dot</i> of Willpower, and can return that point of Memory to a given Arisen in order to get that Willpower dot back?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:45:58-07:00","id":971647,"title":"","content":"Sounds good. Gifts are usually a bit broader than just one power, so I'd give them a set of Auspex and Dominate Devotions. Maybe have one or two use dots in Nightmare. I'm using the Khaibit writeup as a guide. As far as I remember, the Khaibit, the Kerberoi, and the Neglatu are the only canon 2e Bloodlines written up, I'd suggest looking at those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:56:26-07:00","id":971692,"title":"","content":"I got Usiri among my list of Bloodline Conversions. If you're interested, you can go and give it a look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}